{%- comment -%}
  Builds the contact-shadow filter value from a 0-100 strength.

  Two drop-shadows, not one: a tight core where the garment meets the
  surface, and a wide soft one for the falloff. A single layer reads as
  either a sticker or a haze.

  drop-shadow follows the image's alpha channel, so on a cut-out PNG it
  traces the garment. box-shadow would draw a rectangle round the picture.

  Zero returns the literal keyword none rather than a transparent shadow,
  so the browser skips the compositing entirely.

  Accepts:
  - strength: {Number} 0-100

  Usage, inside a style block:
  --ab-shadow: {% render 'abmira-shadow', strength: 45 %};
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign sh = strength | default: 0
  assign core = sh | divided_by: 545.0
  assign soft = sh | divided_by: 300.0
-%}
{%- if sh > 0 -%}
drop-shadow(0 4px 5px rgba(25, 24, 19, {{ core }})) drop-shadow(0 18px 20px rgba(25, 24, 19, {{ soft }}))
{%- else -%}
none
{%- endif -%}
